 "assumptions": [
  "Elevations are apparent azimuth/elevation from NASA/JPL Horizons (QUANTITIES=4) for a topocentric observer on the Moon (coord@301).",
  "Geometric (smooth-sphere) horizon at 0° elevation; LOLA terrain shadowing is not modelled.",
  "Airless observer — Horizons applies no atmospheric refraction.",
  "Sun visibility is evaluated at the solar disc centre (~0.27° angular radius not modelled).",
  "Earth above the geometric horizon is Direct-to-Earth visibility *potential* only — not a link budget, antenna mask, or DSN schedule.",
  "Durations use sample-and-hold over [start_utc, end_utc): each sample at t covers min(step, end - t); a Horizons STOP sample exactly at end contributes 0 h.",
  "Visibility percentages are time-weighted over samples with both Sun and Earth data."
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "Results are NOT a NASA-endorsed landing-safety or flight-operations score.",
  "Without LOLA topography, local ridges can hide the Sun or Earth even when geometric elevation is positive.",
  "Hourly or multi-hour samples are coarse estimates (±1 step); not second-precision event times.",
  "Ties in score produce no single recommendation.",
  "Partial ephemeris coverage downgrades data quality and refuses ranking when missing samples exceed 5%.",
  "Missing ephemeris samples are excluded from duration/percentage denominators (neither counted as visible nor invisible)."
 ],
